WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you guys heard
of the term sharenting?

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.840
-No.
-Er, sharenting? No.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.960
Sharing about being a parent?

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.720
Those parents that share everything
about their children online?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.600
Sharenting.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.360
It's something that I do
quite regularly to be honest.

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.480
People come to this country,
they haven't been back,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.160
they have kids
and make their life here.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.080
Some of my family back home
have never seen them before.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.360
If I didn't put them on social
media they wouldn't see them.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.160
Sometimes I get really embarrassed

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.040
when my mum posts stuff
on her Facebook page

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.000
or her Instagram or whatever,
very embarrassing.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:50.640
Very.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.120
-Very?
-Mmm.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.240
They might not want their friends
to see them that way.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.640
They want to have some kind
of control over their image.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.600
There's a famous case
of Gwyneth Paltrow

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.720
posting a picture of her daughter
Apple and it was a selfie.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.520
There was nothing really, you would
think, contentious about it,

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.720
yet her daughter
complained about it.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.880
Wow, I'd be in trouble.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.720
They're posting about people
who are not themselves

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.800
and that could impact us
when we go out into the real world

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.680
and try to get a job, for example.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.880
There is an element of trust there
between a parent and a child

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.000
I'm not comfortable with
my face being shown

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.520
without me knowing what actually I'm
being perceived as on their platform.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.680
It may not seem like something
which is particularly significant.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.640
It may be very personally
upsetting to individuals

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.400
what parents put up on the internet.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.280
For people of our generation,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.640
your online identity isn't
so much seen as separate

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.720
from your real-life identity
but just an extension of it.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.400
Social media profiles
are identity projects.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.800
I don't think that the government
as well as parents

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.960
should take control
over our online identities

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.040
because it is a part of who we are

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.240
and we use our posts and stuff
like that to express ourselves.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.760
-It draws attention to

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.040
the kind of complex everyday work
that those posts are doing

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.560
which are not about showing off.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.640
Sharenting isn't new. Those of us
that can remember cringy moments

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.800
seeing kids' photo albums
handed around to friends and family

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.000
know all too well that this
is a fairly fundamental urge

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.840
on behalf of parents to share
their pride about their children.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.400
It's a way of showing that
you're doing that parenting.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:41.120
What is new about sharenting in
the digital context is of course that

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.360
we are leaving a fairly extensive
and lengthy digital stream

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.080
of photos, comments, stories.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.600
We didn't want to invade her privacy,
even though she's just a baby.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.960
That's going to stay online forever.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:03.360
Any image you post now is going
to be on the internet forever

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:06.280
and then we don’t know what's
going to happen in the future

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.880
with things coming up like deepfake

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.040
and you're just
giving your kid's image away.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.960
Especially now with
face-recognition software

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.680
by posting facial images online

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.800
you're helping them
create a database.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:39.480
You don’t know how these images that
you've posted are going to be used.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.840
Unfortunately we have
paedophile groups who will literally

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.520
sort of scan videos
to take out single shots

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.000
which seem to expose parts
of a child's body or--

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.400
And that's a horrifying thought

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.520
so I think a lot of this is about
education and changing social norms.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.480
One of the strategies that I use is

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.560
taking pictures of them when they're
not actually facing the camera

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.520
so you can't see her face.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.400
These new digital tools enable
us to look back on

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.680
nice moments from
our child's early days,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.480
early years, development, etc.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.680
Funny little things that you write
on there and then it's like,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.240
"Oh yeah that happened then,
like a whole year ago."

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.080
It's pretty good to let
all her friends know that

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.200
I did this, oh,
I went to this school and like,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.280
knowing that, oh like,
I'm really happy.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.640
If sharenting is done
in a responsible way

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.600
and it enables families
to have conversations,

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.240
for example with their kids
as they get older

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.560
about what you want to have online,
how you portray yourself,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.720
then actually I think it can
be a really important step

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.720
towards keeping kids themselves safe

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.040
as they become
digitally enabled adults.

